===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|ice hockey}} An enclosed bench where a player must remain for timed period (a [[penalty]]) that is assessed after an infraction.
#: {{ux|en|Both players got to cool their heels for five minutes in their respective '''penalty boxes''' after the fight.}}
# {{lb|en|soccer}} The [[penalty area]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Stuart Barnes|title=Swindon stunner for Curbishley|work=The Guardian|date=2000-03-12|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2000/mar/12/match.sport10|issn=0261-3077|passage=At times, Swindon's '''penalty box''' resembled a pinball machine.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|figuratively}} A temporary [[punishment]], or, metaphorically, a similar setback (e.g., loss of control, embarrassment, etc.).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Tim Breithaupt|title=10 Steps to Sales Success: The Proven System That Can Shorten the Selling Cycle, Double Your Close Ratio|isbn=081447165X|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=9yNSqTdMjZ0C&pg=PA174&dq=%22penalty+box%22+-hockey+-football+-soccer&sig=zWYjAqASux2QhQp119WmnxRE5iI#PPA170,M1|page=170
|passage=A visit to the '''penalty box''' occurs when the salesman has relinquished control of the sales call by immediately answering the customer's question.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=John Portmann|title=Sex and heaven: Catholics in bed and at prayer|isbn=0312294883|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=xwNXacL5gtkC&pg=PA155&dq=%22penalty+box%22+-hockey+-football+-soccer&sig=9h4AXhHiftBJezXQ9EwY6UYhqcI|page=155
|passage=What can land you in this metaphorical holding cell, the '''penalty box''' of Catholicism?}}
